# SABOTAGE: MG-17 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — LINK 2 of `Samen.Vault.Change.repo!/1`'s
# three-step chain is severed: `(resource_repo || config_repo) || raise` becomes
# `resource_repo || (config_repo && raise)` (`&&` binds tighter than `||`), so the
# `:samen_core, :vault_repo` FALLBACK stops being a fallback and becomes a trap. A resource
# whose own repo does not resolve — the case the fallback exists for, e.g. a PII-bearing
# resource whose data layer is not the one holding `pii_vault` — raises instead of vaulting.
#
# Invisible whenever the resource resolves its own repo (the `||` short-circuits before the
# mutated conjunction is ever reached), which is why the named red makes the resource's own
# AshPostgres repo unresolvable for the duration of the write, through Spark's own
# configurable-option override, and asserts both halves of the chain's state first.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: LINK 1 (sabotage 340 owns that) and the raise message.
#
# One boolean operator. Touches vault/change.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/vault_change_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-17: when the RESOURCE resolves no repo, the write falls back to :vault_repo
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/vault/change.ex
@@ -275,7 +275,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Vault.Change do
 
   defp repo!(changeset) do
     AshPostgres.DataLayer.Info.repo(changeset.resource, :mutate) ||
-      Application.get_env(:samen_core, :vault_repo) ||
+      Application.get_env(:samen_core, :vault_repo) &&
       raise "Samen.Vault.Change: could not resolve a repo for #{inspect(changeset.resource)}"
   end
 end
